WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.460
Step 1 of our proof focuses on the right-angled triangle Efx.

00:05.060 --> 00:10.880
Because the rear axle line goes straight through the turning center x at a right angle to the side of the car,

00:11.300 --> 00:13.320
the angle at f is 90 degrees.

00:14.040 --> 00:17.680
We know the hypotenuse Ex is the turning radius R,

00:17.840 --> 00:21.280
and the vertical side Ef is the wheelbase L.

00:21.980 --> 00:26.060
Applying Pythagoras' theorem gives us the horizontal distance fx,

00:26.060 --> 00:29.320
the square root of R-squared minus L-squared.

